      en: "Fada Ancient Cave Art is a UNESCO World Heritage site featuring rock paintings from the Neolithic period (c. 6000 BCE). The paintings depict wildlife such as giraffes, elephants, and crocodiles, as well as ceremonial scenes. The pigments were made from ochre and charcoal. Over 500 individual figures have been cataloged across 20 rock shelters. In 2015, a conservation project cleaned and stabilized the most vulnerable panels. The site is accessible only by 4x4 vehicle.",
